      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Diana,\ncan you take a look at this CL which updates how alert messages are sent and adds a Status response to Get_Status messages? I had them as one CL to test the Alert-\u003eGet_Status-\u003eStatus sequence, let me know if you want to split this up into 2 CLs.\n\nThe idea is that to support more alert messages going forward, like go/power-button, the alert needs to be defined where it is triggered. It cannot be defined just using the port\u0027s state, as we do now. This CL creates two functions (pd_broadcast_alert_msg and pd_send_alert_msg) which will allow other parts of the EC to define and send alert messages. For example, battery_v2.c will be able to trigger Battery Status Change alerts, and thermal.c can trigger Operating Condition Change alerts. \n\nThis CL just adds the new functions for sending alerts and a zero\u0027d out Status response. I plan to follow it with CLs to send alerts from different parts of the EC and add the relevant data to the Status response.",
